<!-- filepath: tests/Directory.Build.props

     Belt-and-braces guard for the test projects.

     The root Directory.Build.props already adds tests\** to
     <DefaultItemExcludes> for every project in the tree, and the
     production CookingTime.csproj uses
     <EnableDefaultCompileItems>false</EnableDefaultCompileItems> plus
     an explicit Compile Include list that only references Application/,
     Domain/, and Infrastructure/ - never tests/. This shadowing props
     file is a second layer of defence: any project whose path is at
     or below tests/ inherits these settings even if a future tool
     ignores the root excludes.

     Each test project under tests/ has its own .csproj that lists its
     files explicitly (or relies on the default compile glob after the
     exclude rule above filters tests\** out for the production project).
     We do not disable EnableDefaultCompileItems here because the test
     projects need to pick up their own *.cs files via the default SDK
     glob - we only want to keep them from leaking into the production
     assembly, which the production csproj already prevents. -->
<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <DefaultItemExcludes>$(DefaultItemExcludes);OriginalSource\**;tests\**\*.csproj</DefaultItemExcludes>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>